Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.04,0:01:26.96,Default,,0,0,0,,ONE HUNDRED YEARS OF SOLITUDE
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.25,0:01:57.13,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.29,0:02:01.12,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.92,0:02:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know what you're working on,\Nbut we need to talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.50,0:02:06.42,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a solar weapon, you see?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.29,0:02:10.46,Default,,0,0,0,,A what?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.54,0:02:12.42,Default,,0,0,0,,A weapon\Nthat uses sunlight.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.50,0:02:13.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's the design.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.96,0:02:16.54,Default,,0,0,0,,No gunpowder, Úrsula.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.25,0:02:18.75,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a magnificent idea!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.83,0:02:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,-Magnificent for who?\N-It can be used by an army.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.58,0:02:23.46,Default,,0,0,0,,If I can put on a demonstration,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.67,0:02:26.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I bet I could sell it to the government.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.00,0:02:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I look forward to the day\Nwhen you sell one of your genius ideas
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.54,0:02:32.79,Default,,0,0,0,,that only you understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.54,0:02:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,As news spread\Nabout the quality of the soil,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.38,0:02:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,their tiny village transformed into\Nan active town with stores and workshops,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.71,0:02:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,which lured tradesmen from Arabia…
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.33,0:02:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.25,0:02:50.25,Default,,0,0,0,,…with slippers on their feet\Nand rings in their ears.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.33,0:02:52.16,Default,,0,0,0,,-Matilde!\N-One second!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.71,0:02:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,-Morning.\N-Morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.29,0:02:56.29,Default,,0,0,0,,They're ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.29,0:02:58.79,Default,,0,0,0,,These are good for another year, maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.88,0:03:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,But, Úrsula, tell José Arcadio\Nhe has to stop growing already.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.67,0:03:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.54,0:03:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, please. Don't worry about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.67,0:03:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.67,0:03:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,-Here, candy for you and the children.\N-Ah! Thanks! Just put them over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.33,0:03:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.67,0:03:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm. Listen, these are so good.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.04,0:03:25.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean it, Úrsula. You should sell these.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.75,0:03:28.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Matilde,\Nthere's too much for me to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.92,0:03:29.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Think about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.79,0:03:46.46,Default,,0,0,0,,By March,\Nthe gypsies had returned.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.96,0:04:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Fascinating.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.58,0:04:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,You are a true inventor.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.17,0:04:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Thought you would never return.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.83,0:04:36.16,Default,,0,0,0,,The world is a big place, José Arcadio,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.33,0:04:40.25,Default,,0,0,0,,and it takes some time to traverse it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.88,0:04:43.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Trust me when I say that my plan
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.50,0:04:46.92,Default,,0,0,0,,was always to see you again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.67,0:04:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, show me. Show me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.75,0:04:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Úrsula doesn't want me to say this\Nin front of the children…
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.58,0:05:00.16,Default,,0,0,0,,but I've reached the conclusion
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.58,0:05:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,that the Earth is round,\Nthe same as this orange.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.92,0:05:14.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You think I'm crazy too?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.17,0:05:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Quite the contrary, my friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.79,0:05:19.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I always knew you were an enlightened man…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.88,0:05:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,which is why I have something for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.96,0:05:29.67,Default,,0,0,0,,That noon,\Nas proof of his admiration,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.29,0:05:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades delivered his gift\Nto José Arcadio Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.25,0:05:39.67,Default,,0,0,0,,A gift which would hold profound influence\Nover the future of the village.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.04,0:05:47.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.63,0:05:49.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell your father I'm going to the market!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.58,0:05:59.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Father,\Nmy mother wanted me to tell you--
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.67,0:06:00.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.96,0:06:09.92,Default,,0,0,0,,What's all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.29,0:06:13.04,Default,,0,0,0,,This? This is alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.50,0:06:15.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Alchemy…
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.42,0:06:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The most ancient science in history.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.88,0:06:23.01,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll set up a laboratory\Nso you can experiment with the elements.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.00,0:06:25.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What elements?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.04,0:06:29.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The building blocks of matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.71,0:06:33.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Ammonia. Lead. Mercury.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.17,0:06:35.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And sulfur.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.04,0:06:40.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Alchemy, my friend,\Nis the mastery of matter
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.54,0:06:43.46,Default,,0,0,0,,and the greatest, most splendid power
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.21,0:06:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,that human beings can wield.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.08,0:06:48.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Above this,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.83,0:06:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,there's only God.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.71,0:06:57.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.29,0:06:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano, come here!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.33,0:07:01.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.42,0:07:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,While José Arcadio Buendía devoted himself
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.46,0:07:16.88,Default,,0,0,0,,to the teachings of alchemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.67,0:07:21.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Úrsula was busy developing\Na promising candy-animal confectionery,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.54,0:07:26.58,Default,,0,0,0,,molding her profitable creations\Naround sticks of balsa wood twice a day.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.25,0:07:31.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.67,0:07:43.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, tomorrow…
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.96,0:07:45.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Candy for sale!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.21,0:07:48.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see. We're almost out of lime.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.58,0:07:50.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, where's José Arcadio?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.96,0:08:02.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Those who were closest\Nto José Arcadio Buendía,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.96,0:08:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,who had known him\Nsince the foundation of Macondo,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.00,0:08:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,were startled at how much he had changed\Nunder Melquiades's influence.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.50,0:08:15.08,Default,,0,0,0,,An alchemist's mission\Nis to decipher the mysteries of matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.17,0:08:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,And the ultimate proof\Nof his total mastery
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.29,0:08:20.87,Default,,0,0,0,,is the transformation
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.25,0:08:23.88,Default,,0,0,0,,of common base metals
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.58,0:08:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,into gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.33,0:08:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,That's impossible, Melquiades.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.46,0:08:32.42,Default,,0,0,0,,If it were that easy,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.50,0:08:34.75,Default,,0,0,0,,everybody would have\Nendless quantities of gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.83,0:08:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It is possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.88,0:08:38.51,Default,,0,0,0,,For an alchemist, it's possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.54,0:08:46.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Look.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.00,0:08:52.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It requires a lot of skill and practice.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.25,0:08:55.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I strongly suggest\Nyou start with something simpler.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.54,0:09:02.79,Default,,0,0,0,,TRANSMUTING METALS\NTHE DOUBLING OF GOLD
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.25,0:09:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you imagine\Nwhat we could do with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.25,0:09:10.08,Default,,0,0,0,,-There are no limits.\N-Úrsula, Melquiades is staying for dinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.50,0:09:14.79,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. Help yourself to what's left.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.67,0:09:18.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry about me, thank you.\NI must be on my way.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.04,0:09:20.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm needed back at the camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.96,0:09:21.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Good evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.50,0:09:27.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades, I'd still like for you to come\Ntomorrow morning if that's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.42,0:09:34.75,Default,,0,0,0,,-See you tomorrow?\N-I'm afraid that won't be possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.46,0:09:38.34,Default,,0,0,0,,We're packing up our things.\NWe leave at dawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.29,0:09:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,But we just began with the experiments.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.96,0:09:45.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I know, but you have everything\Nthat you need to keep moving forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.29,0:09:48.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You can do this alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.88,0:09:54.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry.\NI promise I'll be back, my friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.75,0:10:10.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Next time you invite your friend\Nfor a meal,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.63,0:10:12.46,Default,,0,0,0,,ask me if there's enough food first.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.96,0:10:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You're always locked inside that room.\NYou never think.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.50,0:10:17.92,Default,,0,0,0,,For your information,\Nit's an alchemy laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.21,0:10:20.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And by the way…
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.38,0:10:23.55,Default,,0,0,0,,it'll make us very rich.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.63,0:10:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that's great
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.38,0:10:27.51,Default,,0,0,0,,because my inheritance has almost run out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.29,0:10:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio Buendía,\Nforget this nonsense once and for all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.50,0:10:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,We have a family to feed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.00,0:10:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio, Aureliano! Food's ready!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.67,0:11:00.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you seen our children?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.75,0:11:03.58,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.13,0:11:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Over there! It's over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.50,0:11:41.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-Go that way, Aureliano!\N-Okay, okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.00,0:11:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.92,0:12:27.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.46,0:12:43.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Pilar, have you seen my children?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.25,0:12:48.21,Default,,0,0,0,,They left at dawn and haven't returned.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.42,0:12:50.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, I'm sure they're close by.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.13,0:12:55.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry about it. Since you're here,\Nwhy don't you sit down for a reading?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.29,0:13:08.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Ask away.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.25,0:13:10.58,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.71,0:13:13.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Pick three.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.63,0:13:27.59,Default,,0,0,0,,He observes the world differently.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.54,0:13:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,He's a man of passions and obsessions.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.13,0:13:37.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Luckily, he's not interested in\Nwomen or other vices,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.83,0:13:40.75,Default,,0,0,0,,or he'd spend his days drunk\Nat Catarino's.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.79,0:13:43.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, they're gonna get it now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.71,0:13:45.59,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll finish later. Thank you, Pilar!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.92,0:13:48.88,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.46,0:13:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.79,0:14:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,TRANSMUTING METALS\NTHE DOUBLING OF GOLD
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.04,0:14:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,You won't believe\Nwhat the kids brought home with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.88,0:14:20.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me you didn't just take my coins.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.96,0:14:22.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are they?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.58,0:14:25.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I followed the formula step-by-step.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.17,0:14:27.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What formula?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.29,0:14:30.58,Default,,0,0,0,,A process that can\Nscientifically double your gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.42,0:14:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Does that molten blob\Nlook like gold to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.67,0:14:37.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I bet I could separate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.71,0:14:40.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd need to use a bit more sulfur,\Nprobably less lead,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.58,0:14:43.37,Default,,0,0,0,,What made you think you could\Ntake these without asking me?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.46,0:14:46.54,Default,,0,0,0,,You know I need those coins\Nto help me grow my candy business.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.58,0:14:49.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What candies?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.79,0:14:53.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Not only do you do nothing for this house,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.21,0:14:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,you also have the nerve\Nto destroy what little we have left.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.21,0:15:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll recover every last gram of gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.54,0:15:02.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I swear.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.13,0:15:07.38,Default,,0,0,0,,No. I don't need you\Nto recover any of the gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.25,0:15:10.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I just need you\Nto take care of your family.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.58,0:15:13.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Of our children,\Nwho are growing up without a father.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.33,0:15:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,They look like savages. I mean, look.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.25,0:15:35.17,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.42,0:15:37.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.58,0:15:40.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.00,0:15:50.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.21,0:16:09.79,Default,,0,0,0,,From that afternoon on,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.88,0:16:12.76,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio Buendía\Ngave them his best hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.42,0:16:16.63,Default,,0,0,0,,-He taught them how to read and write.\N-It's about patience. Okay, boys?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.71,0:16:18.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And told them about\Nthe wonders of the world…
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.79,0:16:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I caught one!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.83,0:16:23.66,Default,,0,0,0,,…pushing the limits\Nof their imagination to the extreme.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.21,0:16:28.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And eventually,\Nthe boys learned it was possible
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.38,0:16:30.26,Default,,0,0,0,,to cross the Aegean Sea on foot,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.75,0:16:34.63,Default,,0,0,0,,that one could jump from island to island\Nall the way to the port of Salonika.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.71,0:16:36.96,Default,,0,0,0,,…pastime\Nwas to sit and think.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.46,0:16:54.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't even try.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.13,0:16:57.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, these ones are ready to be sold.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.17,0:16:59.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll go get José Arcadio.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.42,0:17:04.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I counted them, so don't think\NI won't notice if you take one.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.54,0:17:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,That morning, when she entered the room,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.79,0:17:21.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Úrsula was struck with a mingled sense\Nof shame and pity at the sight of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.08,0:17:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,He was so well-equipped,\Nit struck her as abnormal.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.92,0:17:30.30,Default,,0,0,0,,And she began to relive\Nher newlywed horrors once more.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.96,0:17:32.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Why that face?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.96,0:17:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Did Prudencio Aguilar's ghost\Nvisit you again?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.83,0:17:40.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-It's worse than that.\N-What could possibly be worse?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.54,0:17:43.37,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.38,0:17:46.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-I saw him naked.\N-And?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.67,0:17:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,His manhood is enormous.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.46,0:17:57.09,Default,,0,0,0,,That's normal, Úrsula! He's growing.\NEverything grows at the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.67,0:17:59.09,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not normal, Pilar.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.04,0:18:01.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Might as well be a deformity.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.79,0:18:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,It's worse than having a tail.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.79,0:18:09.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What if he's forced to spend\Nthe rest of his life alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.96,0:18:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Quite the contrary.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.67,0:18:12.59,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll be lucky.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.92,0:18:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,But if you need reassurance,\NI'm happy to do a reading.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.33,0:18:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.13,0:18:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Cut it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.67,0:18:41.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Relax, José Arcadio. This won't hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.79,0:18:43.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Choose three.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.96,0:18:53.09,Default,,0,0,0,,What's it say?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.25,0:19:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,That you will be unconquerable\Nlike a hurricane.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.38,0:19:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh my word!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.50,0:19:21.88,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio felt\Nhis bones filling up with foam.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.04,0:19:27.62,Default,,0,0,0,,And he experienced a languid fear\Nand a terrible desire to weep.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.38,0:19:32.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What did the cards say?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.63,0:19:36.01,Default,,0,0,0,,His life won't be short\Nin women or descendants.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.25,0:19:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I can assure you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.67,0:20:23.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That night,\Nin the terror of sleeplessness,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.54,0:20:27.33,Default,,0,0,0,,he desired Pilar Ternera again\Nwith a brutal anxiety.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.88,0:20:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,,He wanted to be with her…
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.04,0:20:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,for them to never leave the granary,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.46,0:20:42.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and for her to say, "Oh my word."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.71,0:21:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm. Wednesday.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.88,0:22:34.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh! Uh!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.04,0:22:45.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Pilar Ternera\Nhad permitted him to understand
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.42,0:22:48.25,Default,,0,0,0,,the reason that men fear death.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.21,0:22:53.54,Default,,0,0,0,,-Good morning.\N-What flavors do you have?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.63,0:22:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,-Tamarind, corozo, lime, and orange.\N-I'll have some orange and corozo.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.88,0:22:57.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.92,0:22:59.80,Default,,0,0,0,,-How are things today?\N-Pilar!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.29,0:23:01.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Business is good, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.50,0:23:02.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We can't even keep up now.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.13,0:23:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Stay here with the children.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.29,0:23:07.58,Default,,0,0,0,,-I'll go home and bring more candy.\N-Of course. Go.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.67,0:23:10.55,Default,,0,0,0,,-One lime and one corozo, please.\N-Go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.08,0:23:14.58,Default,,0,0,0,,-Could I have an orange one?\N-The orange one is scrumptious.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.50,0:23:19.46,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio… pass me the candy.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.00,0:23:47.38,Default,,0,0,0,,-Where were you?\N-Sh.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.79,0:23:54.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not the first time\NI've seen you leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.08,0:24:01.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, what is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.00,0:24:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I met a woman.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.79,0:24:11.75,Default,,0,0,0,,A woman? What were you doing with a woman?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.83,0:24:14.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean,\Nwhat was she doing with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.50,0:24:20.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Her skin smells just like smoke…
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.13,0:24:31.30,Default,,0,0,0,,and her laughter scares the doves away.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.33,0:24:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,When she touches me,\Nit's… almost as if she knows my whole body
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.96,0:24:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,better than I do myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.71,0:24:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't imagine all the things
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.08,0:24:47.41,Default,,0,0,0,,you can accomplish\Nwith a tongue, Aureliano.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:48.58,0:24:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You wouldn't believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:52.38,0:24:53.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.79,0:24:57.54,Default,,0,0,0,,We reached a moment\Nwhere we nearly fainted
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.63,0:24:58.88,Default,,0,0,0,,from all of the pleasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.50,0:25:04.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.08,0:25:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,What's it feel like?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.54,0:25:17.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Like the whole world is shaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.21,0:25:26.88,Default,,0,0,0,,The sun's rays\Nconverge at the lens,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.25,0:25:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,and when projected,\Nthey can burn the target.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.08,0:25:44.87,Default,,0,0,0,,By concentrating them\Nin one spot,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.79,0:25:48.21,Default,,0,0,0,,they'll make that vessel\Nburst into flames.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.42,0:26:12.05,Default,,0,0,0,,-Yeah! Mother!\N-That's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.96,0:26:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you see that, Úrsula? We did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:21.00,0:26:21.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It works.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:24.13,0:26:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Many years later,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.04,0:26:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,seconds before the army officer\Ngave the command to fire,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.38,0:26:32.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel Aureliano Buendía relived\Nthat warm March afternoon,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.04,0:26:34.83,Default,,0,0,0,,when his father interrupted his lesson,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.92,0:26:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,to listen to the distant pipes and drums\Nof the returning gypsies.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:38.83,0:26:39.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.13,0:27:11.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Come! Come!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:12.38,0:27:13.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Come closer!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.17,0:27:18.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And see the most recent discovery\Nof the wise men of Memphis!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.00,0:27:23.88,Default,,0,0,0,,The wonder that belonged to King Solomon!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:27.38,0:27:29.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, 30 reales, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.96,0:28:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The chest gave off\Na glacial exhalation.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:15.92,0:28:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Inside, was an enormous transparent block
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.00,0:28:21.79,Default,,0,0,0,,with an infinite number\Nof internal needles,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.42,0:28:27.30,Default,,0,0,0,,in which the light of the sunset\Nwas broken up into colored stars.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.38,0:28:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The biggest diamond in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.79,0:28:30.62,Default,,0,0,0,,No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.33,0:28:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It's ice.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.38,0:28:43.05,Default,,0,0,0,,-This is the great invention of our time.\N-Uh, uh, uh!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:43.88,0:28:46.26,Default,,0,0,0,,That's five reales more\Nif you want to touch it.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:20.29,0:29:21.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.13,0:29:23.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It's boiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.63,0:29:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:25.21,0:29:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,THE MAGNIFICENT WONDERS\NOF THE WISE MEN OF MEMPHIS
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.54,0:29:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Experience the power\Nof the Sumerian potion
Dialogue: 0,0:29:40.46,0:29:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,that was kept in obscurity for centuries.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.83,0:29:48.75,Default,,0,0,0,,THE RENOWNED EUCLIDES
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.83,0:29:49.96,Default,,0,0,0,,A thick syrup
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.21,0:29:54.79,Default,,0,0,0,,to make oneself… invisible.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.88,0:29:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.71,0:30:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, sir.\NYou know Melquiades, the alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:02.17,0:30:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades is gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:04.58,0:30:06.50,Default,,0,0,0,,He perished in the dunes of Singapore.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.50,0:30:11.79,Default,,0,0,0,,That can't be true.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.88,0:30:14.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades, he can't have died…
Dialogue: 0,0:31:13.38,0:31:14.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades passed away.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:41.83,0:31:45.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Keeping alchemy alive is now\Nthe best way to honor his memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:10.96,0:32:11.92,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.92,0:32:28.42,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio…
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.33,0:33:09.00,Default,,0,0,0,,One Thursday in January,\Nat two o'clock in the morning,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.08,0:33:10.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Amaranta was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:12.13,0:33:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Úrsula examined her carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:15.38,0:33:17.96,Default,,0,0,0,,She was light and watery, like a newt.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.50,0:33:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,But all of her parts were human.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.04,0:33:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,-She's so pretty.\N-Finally, the daughter you yearned for.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.17,0:33:39.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-She hasn't cried, not once.\N-That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:40.04,0:33:41.17,Default,,0,0,0,,She'll be a very serene girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:41.25,0:33:43.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Yes, congratulations.\N-Hey, this cookie's amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.04,0:33:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,-From the shop.\N-Have some bread.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.67,0:33:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:46.63,0:33:48.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I made this myself. It's honey bread.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.79,0:33:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-Mm, so good.\N-So, where's your husband?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:51.92,0:33:53.46,Default,,0,0,0,,In his workshop, I would guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:53.54,0:33:55.08,Default,,0,0,0,,-Oh, let me hold her.\N-He won't be long.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.17,0:33:56.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-And then me.\N-Right…
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.50,0:33:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,We did it!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:58.00,0:33:59.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-Úrsula!\N-Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:59.54,0:34:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Úrsula!\N-Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:02.04,0:34:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-Sh, sh, sh, sh.\N-We have guests.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.54,0:34:05.46,Default,,0,0,0,,The tiger came down\Nfrom the mountain!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.54,0:34:07.50,Default,,0,0,0,,We thought you had died.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:07.58,0:34:09.96,Default,,0,0,0,,My friends. Magnífico, Gerineldo.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:11.08,0:34:13.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-I have here some gold coins.\N-Sh, sh, sh.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:13.88,0:34:15.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Recovered from an impossible alloy.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:17.17,0:34:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this true?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.08,0:34:21.33,Default,,0,0,0,,-Yes, it is.\N-You have no idea how happy I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:22.21,0:34:23.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.17,0:34:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,-How many goats is that?\N-Set up shop!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:25.63,0:34:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Sh! Quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.67,0:34:28.42,Default,,0,0,0,,My son, how about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.92,0:34:31.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks more like dog poop.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.83,0:34:32.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Watch your mouth!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:43.63,0:34:44.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, let's eat.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:45.29,0:34:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-I'll pour us a drink.\N-Juice.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:47.33,0:34:49.04,Default,,0,0,0,,How are you? Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:49.13,0:34:51.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Little baby! Little Amaranta…
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.58,0:34:55.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Come in. My brothers are out.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:57.42,0:35:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,He humiliates me!\NHe keeps treating me like a little boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:03.08,0:35:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't let\Nthese silly things get to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.17,0:35:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't spend another second\Ninside the laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:12.21,0:35:13.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll live life my own way.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:17.38,0:35:18.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Easy now.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.50,0:35:28.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you just tell your father\Nwhat you actually want?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:35.71,0:35:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,What I want
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.42,0:35:38.34,Default,,0,0,0,,is to be with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:56.38,0:35:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, me too.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:22.79,0:36:25.75,Default,,0,0,0,,FOR THE FIRST TIME IN THE AMERICAS\NTHE MAGIC CARPET
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.67,0:36:28.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:42.33,0:36:45.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That doesn't compare\Nto how I feel when you and I together.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.25,0:36:52.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, you're a grown man.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.83,0:36:59.91,Default,,0,0,0,,We're having a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.67,0:37:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,SHOWS
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.04,0:37:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:38.50,0:37:39.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.71,0:37:43.96,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.33,0:37:46.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Leave me alone!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:06.13,0:38:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio lost his appetite\Nand could not sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:11.58,0:38:16.29,Default,,0,0,0,,He was so disturbed, anxious, and bitten\Nby a hostile rancor against the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:17.54,0:38:21.33,Default,,0,0,0,,that he left his bed that night\Nto mingle in the confusion of the fair
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.38,0:38:24.09,Default,,0,0,0,,and find some solace.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.42,0:38:34.80,Default,,0,0,0,,After wandering around among\Nall kinds of contraptions,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:36.00,0:38:37.75,Default,,0,0,0,,he spotted a young gypsy girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.29,0:38:41.62,Default,,0,0,0,,She was the most beautiful woman\Nhe had ever seen in his life.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:57.71,0:38:59.59,Default,,0,0,0,,On first contact with her body,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:00.38,0:39:02.92,Default,,0,0,0,,the girl's bones seemed\Nto become disjointed
Dialogue: 0,0:39:03.00,0:39:05.17,Default,,0,0,0,,with a disorderly crunch,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.25,0:39:07.13,Default,,0,0,0,,like the sound of a box of dominoes.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:07.21,0:39:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.75,0:39:13.96,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, kids. Get up.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:16.88,0:39:17.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's your brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:18.96,0:39:20.09,Default,,0,0,0,,He hasn't returned.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.42,0:39:35.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Matilde?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.54,0:39:39.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you seen my son?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:41.79,0:39:42.79,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:42.88,0:39:44.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Last time I saw him was at your house.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:44.83,0:39:46.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe let's ask Pilar?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.83,0:39:54.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Pilar!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.13,0:39:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you seen José Arcadio?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.25,0:40:08.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Catarino!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:12.42,0:40:15.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-Catarino, have you seen my son?\N-Your son? No.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:15.33,0:40:17.29,Default,,0,0,0,,He was with the gypsies last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:46.58,0:40:47.58,Default,,0,0,0,,He's a gypsy now.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:52.54,0:40:54.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Off you go. Run back home, all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:55.38,0:40:56.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell your father what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:20.00,0:41:22.75,Default,,0,0,0,,In a few hours,\NJosé Arcadio Buendía gathered
Dialogue: 0,0:41:22.83,0:41:24.33,Default,,0,0,0,,a group of well-equipped men.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.54,0:41:46.87,Default,,0,0,0,,After three days of useless searching,\Nthey returned to the village.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:46.08,0:42:49.58,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio Buendía\Nwas consumed by consternation
Dialogue: 0,0:42:49.67,0:42:50.80,Default,,0,0,0,,for several weeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:21.75,0:43:24.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Silver is best worked within filaments.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:26.17,0:43:27.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll show you how.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.83,0:43:38.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry, my son.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:39.54,0:43:40.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Your brother will come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:43.79,0:43:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.79,0:43:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Grab the hammer.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:52.04,0:43:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,We gotta hammer the silver\Nto give it shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:58.13,0:43:58.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:39.42,0:44:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Time put things in their place.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:51.21,0:44:53.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Father! The basket!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:54.42,0:44:55.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:56.71,0:44:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-Father!\N-That's the properties of matter, son.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:59.00,0:45:01.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing extraordinary,\Nonce you understand it.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:06.04,0:45:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,During his prolonged confinement,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:08.75,0:45:11.38,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio begged with all of his heart
Dialogue: 0,0:45:11.46,0:45:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,that the long-awaited miracle\Nwould not be turning metals into gold,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.88,0:45:18.38,Default,,0,0,0,,but Úrsula's return.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:49.79,0:45:51.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Father! Look over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:01.38,0:46:03.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Almost five months later,\NÚrsula returned.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.00,0:46:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It's your mama. Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:06.00,0:46:08.63,Default,,0,0,0,,She came from\Nthe other side of the great swamp,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:08.71,0:46:11.38,Default,,0,0,0,,where there were towns\Nthat received mail every month
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.46,0:46:14.63,Default,,0,0,0,,and where they were familiar\Nwith the implements of good living.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.17,0:46:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's José Arcadio?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.21,0:46:31.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I never did find their tracks, son.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:32.88,0:46:34.34,Default,,0,0,0,,And nobody else has seen him.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:02.00,0:47:02.88,Default,,0,0,0,,My little girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:14.75,0:47:16.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are all these people?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:22.08,0:47:24.87,Default,,0,0,0,,They all wanted to see\Nthe marvel of this small town
Dialogue: 0,0:47:25.42,0:47:26.80,Default,,0,0,0,,in the middle of the swamp.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:28.46,0:47:29.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You really did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:30.54,0:47:33.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You found the path\Nthat connects Macondo with the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:38.54,0:47:40.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to introduce\NVisitación and Cataure.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:42.17,0:47:43.84,Default,,0,0,0,,My companions during the journey.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:44.79,0:47:46.12,Default,,0,0,0,,They're moving in with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:51.42,0:47:53.38,Default,,0,0,0,,-Welcome.\N-Thank you for having us.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:57.75,0:47:59.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Pleased to meet you.\N-Welcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:12.33,0:48:13.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:06.96,0:49:08.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't ever leave again.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:10.63,0:49:11.76,Default,,0,0,0,,You better not either.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:21.38,0:49:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Pilar.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:26.13,0:49:27.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Is everything all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:34.33,0:49:35.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, whose child is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.38,0:49:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It's mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.08,0:49:41.33,Default,,0,0,0,,A boy, actually.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:41.42,0:49:42.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And his father?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.75,0:49:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,It's José Arcadio's.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:48.96,0:49:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm here to give him to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.42,0:49:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Pilar, what is this nonsense?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:56.96,0:49:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,We fell in love, Úrsula.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:00.33,0:50:01.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.88,0:50:04.05,Default,,0,0,0,,But we did.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:04.13,0:50:06.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Sh. I'm sorr… All right. Sh.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.21,0:50:07.63,Default,,0,0,0,,So It was you.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:09.33,0:50:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the reason my son\Ndisappeared that day.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:14.88,0:50:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,If you coerced him with witchcraft\Nto give you a son,
Dialogue: 0,0:50:19.92,0:50:21.80,Default,,0,0,0,,that bastard is yours to raise.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:24.46,0:50:25.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, just look.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.46,0:50:27.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I beg you.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:28.79,0:50:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,This boy is your flesh and blood.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:34.96,0:50:36.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Sh, sh, sh, sh.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:39.71,0:50:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,He has the eyes of our fathers.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:41.79,0:50:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no. There, there.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:43.63,0:50:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Sh, sh, sh, sh, sh.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:45.79,0:50:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,A Buendía needs to be\Nraised with his family.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.21,0:50:49.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we'll raise him as our own.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:51.42,0:50:54.63,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as that whore\Nnever steps foot inside this house
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.42,0:50:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,and this child never knows his mother,
Dialogue: 0,0:50:57.38,0:51:00.21,Default,,0,0,0,,because her actions\Nhave brought shame into this family.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:03.63,0:51:05.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You heard our conditions, Pilar.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:09.83,0:51:11.33,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll have a better life here.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:27.88,0:51:30.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The baby was given\Nthe name of José Arcadio,
Dialogue: 0,0:51:31.46,0:51:34.34,Default,,0,0,0,,but they called him "Arcadio"\Nso as to avoid confusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:52.83,0:51:55.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano spent endless hours\Nin the laboratory,
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.50,0:52:00.75,Default,,0,0,0,,learning the art of silverwork\Nby his own experimentation.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:07.75,0:52:10.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Adolescence had taken\Nthe softness from his voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:11.71,0:52:12.88,Default,,0,0,0,,He became silent,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.29,0:52:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,perpetually solitary.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:19.71,0:52:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And yet, it had restored\Nthe intense expression
Dialogue: 0,0:52:22.58,0:52:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,that he had in his eyes when he was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:35.25,0:52:36.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's play!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:37.54,0:52:38.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:39.17,0:52:40.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Go hide!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:41.04,0:52:42.54,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:42.63,0:52:44.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha! Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:00.25,0:53:01.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:03.33,0:53:05.37,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:06.96,0:53:08.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-Run!\N-Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:09.75,0:53:10.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:11.88,0:53:13.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Go hide!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:15.08,0:53:15.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:16.46,0:53:17.63,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:21.67,0:53:23.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Arcadio, Amaranta!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:23.38,0:53:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't wanna\Nhear you speaking Wayuu.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.46,0:53:27.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you to please speak English.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:30.04,0:53:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.13,0:53:36.13,Default,,0,0,0,,They're almost here.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:48.79,0:53:51.08,Default,,0,0,0,,BASED ON THE NOVEL\NBY GABRIEL GARCÍA MÁRQUEZ
